      "id": "vdwrw5b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.1 Primary Memory (Main Memory)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Primary memory is directly accessible by the CPU for processing instructions.",
        "RAM is temporary and volatile, losing contents when power is turned off.",
        "ROM is non-volatile and permanently stores essential startup software like BIOS.",
        "Cache memory bridges CPU and RAM to accelerate access to frequently used data.",
        "Secondary memory offers mass, non-volatile long-term storage for files and programs."
      ],
      "id": "ry1z0to"
    },
